  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Consider the function <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> defined by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. Consider the statements<br/>(I) The curve <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> intersects the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis exactly at one point<br/>(II) The curve <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> intersects the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>cos</mi><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>12</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Then</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Only (II) is correct",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Both (I) and (II) are incorrect",
      "is_correct": false
